hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"220","\Do not make my grave a place of ritual celebration"," but pray for Allah's blessings upon me"," for your blessings reach me from wherever you are. Reference: Abu Dawud 2/218"," Ahmad 2/367. Al-Albani graded it authentic in Sahih Abu Dawud 2/383."""
"221","Wa qāla ṣallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam: \Al-bakhīlu man dhukirtu ʿindahu fa-lam yuṣalli ʿalayya.\"". The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: \""The miser is the one in whose presence I am mentioned"," yet he does not send blessings upon me.\"""""
